      "rev_n_4_66bbe3_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_66bbe3_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_66bbe3",
        "thought_text": "Optimize the prefix sum calculation by using a binary indexed tree (BIT) or Fenwick tree to efficiently query and update prefix sums. This can significantly reduce the time complexity for calculating prefix sums in each iteration.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "823611047629628117",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794400429.427874
      },
      "rev_n_5_b3e065_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_b3e065_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_b3e065",
        "thought_text": "Instead of recalculating the prefix sums from scratch in each iteration, maintain a running total of the prefix sums. This way, each new prefix sum can be computed in constant time relative to the previous one.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "823611047629628117",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794400429.42793
      },
      "rev_n_6_ea9d03_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_ea9d03_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_ea9d03",
        "thought_text": "Analyze the growth pattern of the prefix sums to predict when a value will exceed k. If the prefix sums grow linearly or exponentially, use mathematical formulas to determine the minimum i without iterating through all arrays.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "823611047629628117",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794400429.427941
